   "text": "The drawing shows valganciclovir, the L-valine ester of ganciclovir. I read it in three parts.\n\n- **Purine part:** a guanine-type ring system, with a C=O and an NH in the six-membered ring, an NH2 on the carbon between the ring nitrogens, and N9 of the five-membered ring carrying the side chain.\n- **Side chain:** N\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH(CH2OH)\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O), so the central CH carries one free hydroxymethyl and one ester-linked CH2.\n- **Amino acid part:** the ester carbonyl joins an \u03b1-carbon bearing NH2 and an isopropyl group.\n\nStereochemistry: only the \u03b1-carbon has a wedge, on the NH2 bond. With the implicit H pointing away, the priority order N > C(=O)O > isopropyl runs counterclockwise, so the centre is S, which is L-valine. In SMILES this is `CC(C)[C@H](N)C(=O)O...`. The side-chain CH is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)[C@H](N)C(=O)OCC(CO)OCn1cnc2c1nc(N)[nH]c2=O"
